## Confirmed first blocker

[Diagnostic run 34363848352](https://github.com/saidi19/lumi-model/actions/runs/34363848352),
attempt 1, job `102507402716`, completed successfully. Linux source preflight,
accepted-software acquisition/hash verification, the one inspect diagnostic,
owned-input retirement and small evidence upload all passed. Acquisition ran
14:28:49Z–14:30:10Z; the native diagnostic ran 14:30:10Z–14:30:39Z. There was no
retry, rebuild, pull or invocation of the previous guardian attempt.

The diagnostic result is **not an admission pass**:

- `status=passed` means the diagnostic completed and its closed-schema result
  was validated.
- `admission_passed=false`, `code=profile_rejected`.
- `phase=configuration`, `predicate=configuration_labels_equal`.
- The image has a present `Labels` field whose value is `null`.
- The created container has a present `Labels` field whose value is an empty
  dictionary `{}`; no label strings or values were retained.

The old verifier compares canonical JSON for every configuration field. Thus
`null` and `{}` fail that exact equality predicate. This is the observed first
blocker, not a guessed mismatch. The retained booleans establish the exact two
shapes; no raw inspect response or exception text was stored.
This proves the first rejection in this fresh diagnostic; it does not
retrospectively prove the exact cause of the earlier opaque guardian report.

Inference from the unchanged predicate order: earlier runtime/image/container
metadata checks and equality checks for `Env`, `Entrypoint`, `Cmd`, `User` and
`WorkingDir` completed before `Labels` rejected. These are trusted-daemon
metadata observations, not proof of running containment. Later configuration
predicates and all export/rootfs/guardian/worker checks were **not reached**.
There is no claim that this is the only remaining defect.

## Scope and cleanup

Exactly the accepted image was loaded and one container was created, never
started. There was no export, extraction, cgroup, adapter, worker, GPU,
inference, model/data/S3 access or SFT. No software binding or continuation was
released. The source-bound verifier retains the old predicate expressions and
short-circuit order; no admission/profile/parser policy changed.

This run explicitly attests cleanup: after single removal attempts, successful
bounded inventory observations found the owned image and container absent;
owned root files/directories were retired. The separate input receipt attests
one downloaded input file and one input directory retired by exact identities.
Cleanup is verified under the trusted-host/exclusive-daemon premises; there is
no broader host-cleanliness or hostile-root claim.

All old source/evidence remains byte-for-byte unchanged. The previous guardian
workflow did not trigger; old OCI release run `34363848256` was skipped. No old
failed run or artifact was deleted.

